{"vid":"ayAOpko1dtA","source":"ayAOpko1dtA.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.3,"txt":"MIG welder settings can feel like black"},{"t":2.3,"txt":"magic and people are always asking for"},{"t":4.1,"txt":"the secret sauce, but the reality is"},{"t":6,"txt":"there's a wide range of settings that"},{"t":7.6,"txt":"will work in most situations."},{"t":10.2,"txt":"Hey, welcome to the shop. So, we're"},{"t":11.6,"txt":"going to look at one joint with three"},{"t":15.4,"txt":"different"},{"t":16.8,"txt":"settings and techniques here on this"},{"t":20,"txt":"weld. So, we're going to start off by"},{"t":22.1,"txt":"running hot and fast in a straight line"},{"t":24.8,"txt":"using the recommended settings on my"},{"t":27,"txt":"Fronius. Most European machines like"},{"t":29,"txt":"this one recommend higher settings than"},{"t":32.7,"txt":"most American machines and I kind of"},{"t":34.6,"txt":"like how those run. So, I have some"},{"t":37.1,"txt":"1/8-in thick coupons here, just mild"},{"t":39.6,"txt":"steel that I'm tacking up in this"},{"t":41.1,"txt":"T-joint configuration. I just like to"},{"t":43,"txt":"put a tack on each end there. And you"},{"t":45.9,"txt":"could run a push angle, you could run a"},{"t":49,"txt":"drag angle, either way works with short"},{"t":50.9,"txt":"circuit MIG, but I prefer a push angle"},{"t":53.3,"txt":"when I'm working in a straight line like"},{"t":55.7,"txt":"this. I find it easier to watch and stay"},{"t":58.5,"txt":"up on the leading edge of that puddle,"},{"t":60.4,"txt":"and that's really what I'm trying to do."},{"t":62,"txt":"Almost like picture putting your finger"},{"t":64.5,"txt":"on the surface of water as you fill up a"},{"t":66.3,"txt":"glass. That's where I like to keep it"},{"t":69.2,"txt":"and then I can just pace my travel speed"},{"t":71.9,"txt":"to size my fillet weld. See, so if I I"},{"t":74.6,"txt":"had a little bit lower setting, I'd be"},{"t":76,"txt":"traveling a little bit slower to get the"},{"t":78,"txt":"same size weld, but it came out pretty"},{"t":80.7,"txt":"good. So, this gave a nice smooth result"},{"t":83.8,"txt":"and I like the looks of those and I like"},{"t":85.8,"txt":"a smooth continuous weld like this"},{"t":87.6,"txt":"because you're very unlikely to have"},{"t":90.6,"txt":"internal defects and this only took"},{"t":92.6,"txt":"about 21 seconds to run the entire weld,"},{"t":96.2,"txt":"so it's"},{"t":97.9,"txt":"you know, good for production, too."},{"t":100.9,"txt":"Now, let's turn this way down and run"},{"t":104.4,"txt":"technique that's pretty common on TikTok"},{"t":107.3,"txt":"and Instagram Reels and things like"},{"t":109,"txt":"that. We're setting it at 200 in per"},{"t":111.8,"txt":"minute, which is going to drop our"},{"t":113.1,"txt":"amperage down from 150 amps down to 100"},{"t":117.8,"txt":"and we'll just let the synergic voltage"},{"t":119.8,"txt":"follow. One difference you might notice"},{"t":121.9,"txt":"right off the bat is that I'm using a"},{"t":123.3,"txt":"drag angle this time, and that's because"},{"t":125.3,"txt":"I'm using some manipulation to spread"},{"t":127.4,"txt":"out the weld with these colder settings,"},{"t":129.4,"txt":"and I've found that a drag angle is more"},{"t":131.6,"txt":"effective for that. Now, the"},{"t":133.5,"txt":"manipulation that I'm using is to move"},{"t":136,"txt":"up to the root of the joint and then up"},{"t":138.2,"txt":"and down across to fill it in and spread"},{"t":142,"txt":"out that weld bead. And this can be"},{"t":144.8,"txt":"pretty effective if you want to run a"},{"t":146.2,"txt":"stack of dimes, or if you're welding on"},{"t":149,"txt":"material that's a little bit thicker"},{"t":150.6,"txt":"than the capability of your machine,"},{"t":152.5,"txt":"like with a little 120-V MIG. If you"},{"t":154.6,"txt":"want to go on thicker material, this can"},{"t":156.7,"txt":"give you an option to do it. And you do"},{"t":160.2,"txt":"get uh a lot of time for that heat to"},{"t":163,"txt":"really burn into your material, and it"},{"t":165.1,"txt":"can give you a sound weld, but each time"},{"t":167.5,"txt":"you go through that manipulation,"},{"t":169.3,"txt":"there's an opportunity for a lack of"},{"t":171.1,"txt":"fusion defect, where if it's on"},{"t":172.9,"txt":"something that vibrates around, you"},{"t":174.3,"txt":"could have a crack start there. So, you"},{"t":176.8,"txt":"do get that stack of dimes. I'm not the"},{"t":178.5,"txt":"most practiced at it cuz I typically run"},{"t":180.8,"txt":"hot and fast in a straight line. Let's"},{"t":183,"txt":"compare these. In a lot of applications,"},{"t":185,"txt":"either one would work without any issue,"},{"t":187,"txt":"but if you are welding to a code and you"},{"t":188.8,"txt":"need to pass inspection, those little"},{"t":191.3,"txt":"areas where it isn't tied in uh are"},{"t":194.2,"txt":"going to be a lot harder, and you have a"},{"t":196,"txt":"lot of opportunity for lack of fusion"},{"t":197.6,"txt":"defects that you don't have on that. So,"},{"t":199.2,"txt":"on code work, I'd recommend hot and"},{"t":201.5,"txt":"fast. So, that weld took about twice as"},{"t":204.3,"txt":"long to make, and the slower overall"},{"t":207.7,"txt":"progression leads to a lot more heat"},{"t":210.6,"txt":"going into the material. The additional"},{"t":212.4,"txt":"heat input is going to uh cause a little"},{"t":215.9,"txt":"bit more distortion most of the time or"},{"t":217.8,"txt":"warping of your parts. And um"},{"t":220.8,"txt":"combine that with the slower"},{"t":221.8,"txt":"productivity, and then each one of those"},{"t":224,"txt":"movements gives you the opportunity to"},{"t":226.7,"txt":"have a lack of fusion defect in there,"},{"t":228.8,"txt":"where cracks could start. I see a lot of"},{"t":231.6,"txt":"drawbacks to running low and slow and a"},{"t":233.8,"txt":"lot of advantages to running hot and"},{"t":235.6,"txt":"fast, but I'm not going to say one is"},{"t":237.4,"txt":"right or wrong, but I will say that"},{"t":240.2,"txt":"there is some middle ground. And I'm"},{"t":242.2,"txt":"going to crank this up to 300 in per"},{"t":244.2,"txt":"minute, which is more like what Miller"},{"t":246.3,"txt":"would recommend on their weld"},{"t":248,"txt":"calculators. And that'll allow me to run"},{"t":250.6,"txt":"a little bit of manipulation, but it'll"},{"t":252.6,"txt":"still keep a cohesive weld puddle. So,"},{"t":255,"txt":"notice as I run this next one, I'm going"},{"t":257.3,"txt":"to have some manipulation, but I'm not"},{"t":259.4,"txt":"ever leaving the weld puddle."},{"t":261.6,"txt":"Once again, I'm using a drag angle"},{"t":263.3,"txt":"because I'm performing some of that same"},{"t":265.4,"txt":"manipulation, a very similar movement,"},{"t":267.5,"txt":"but the difference this time is that"},{"t":269.8,"txt":"weld puddle is larger, and so I'm never"},{"t":272.4,"txt":"really leaving it. I just advance it and"},{"t":275,"txt":"then spread out a little bit. Almost"},{"t":277,"txt":"like a whip and pause with a little up"},{"t":279.4,"txt":"and down to it. And this can work really"},{"t":281.8,"txt":"well. I'm also moving a lot faster than"},{"t":284,"txt":"that last example, though a little"},{"t":285.4,"txt":"slower than the first. And in the end,"},{"t":288.8,"txt":"it's pretty nice result. Not consistent"},{"t":291,"txt":"again, I don't practice this very often,"},{"t":292.8,"txt":"but it works. Now, that weld did take"},{"t":295.1,"txt":"longer than the first one, about 28"},{"t":296.8,"txt":"seconds versus 21 seconds. But under"},{"t":299,"txt":"powder coat, you will see some ripples"},{"t":300.9,"txt":"there if that's important to you. And"},{"t":302.5,"txt":"that can help to pace progression if you"},{"t":305.2,"txt":"like that. Let me point out a few things"},{"t":307.8,"txt":"looking at all of them together here."},{"t":309.8,"txt":"First of all, you can see that heat tint"},{"t":311.7,"txt":"is by far the largest on low and slow,"},{"t":314.2,"txt":"and then it tapers down and it's much"},{"t":316.6,"txt":"smaller when I'm running hot and fast."},{"t":318.9,"txt":"And notice how well the"},{"t":321.6,"txt":"weld ties in when I'm running hot and"},{"t":323.6,"txt":"fast or even in the middle case where"},{"t":325.7,"txt":"it's not tied in nearly as well on that"},{"t":328.8,"txt":"low and slow option. So, either of these"},{"t":331.4,"txt":"hotter two I would prefer, but you can"},{"t":334.4,"txt":"run low and slow if you need to for"},{"t":336.8,"txt":"whatever reason. Now, as far as testing"},{"t":338.6,"txt":"goes, if I were to take cross sections,"},{"t":340.3,"txt":"I'd have to take a lot of them to really"},{"t":342,"txt":"hit every part of that manipulation. And"},{"t":345.5,"txt":"it depends a lot on technique, but I"},{"t":347.4,"txt":"will bend them open just make sure"},{"t":349.2,"txt":"there's no red flags here. You can't"},{"t":351.4,"txt":"learn a lot from a fillet weld break"},{"t":352.7,"txt":"test on this thin material cuz it just"},{"t":354.3,"txt":"bends open every time. But,"},{"t":357,"txt":"any of them would be acceptable for a"},{"t":359.4,"txt":"lot of situations. So, what would I"},{"t":361,"txt":"recommend? I'd recommend running hot and"},{"t":363.3,"txt":"fast in a straight line. If you are just"},{"t":365.7,"txt":"starting out and it's hard to keep up"},{"t":367.4,"txt":"with the speed at like the 350 in per"},{"t":370,"txt":"minute we were running, you can run 280"},{"t":372.4,"txt":"to 300 and do a very similar technique"},{"t":376.9,"txt":"and come out with a good outcome there,"},{"t":378.7,"txt":"too. If you are just starting out"},{"t":380.6,"txt":"learning welding, I have some affordable"},{"t":382.5,"txt":"online courses linked down in the"},{"t":384,"txt":"description where I'll walk you through"},{"t":385.8,"txt":"in a step-by-step way that helps people"},{"t":388.2,"txt":"to learn way faster. And if you want a"},{"t":391.3,"txt":"full walk-through of how to really dial"},{"t":393.7,"txt":"in your wire speed and voltage settings,"},{"t":395.8,"txt":"check out this video right here."}],"words":[{"t":0.32,"w":"MIG"},{"t":0.52,"w":"welder"},{"t":0.8,"w":"settings"},{"t":1.28,"w":"can"},{"t":1.48,"w":"feel"},{"t":1.72,"w":"like"},{"t":1.96,"w":"black"},{"t":2.32,"w":"magic"},{"t":2.8,"w":"and"},{"t":2.92,"w":"people"},{"t":3.16,"w":"are"},{"t":3.28,"w":"always"},{"t":3.56,"w":"asking"},{"t":3.96,"w":"for"},{"t":4.08,"w":"the"},{"t":4.16,"w":"secret"},{"t":4.56,"w":"sauce,"},{"t":5,"w":"but"},{"t":5.12,"w":"the"},{"t":5.24,"w":"reality"},{"t":5.76,"w":"is"},{"t":6,"w":"there's"},{"t":6.2,"w":"a"},{"t":6.28,"w":"wide"},{"t":6.68,"w":"range"},{"t":6.88,"w":"of"},{"t":7,"w":"settings"},{"t":7.44,"w":"that"},{"t":7.56,"w":"will"},{"t":7.68,"w":"work"},{"t":8.08,"w":"in"},{"t":8.24,"w":"most"},{"t":8.52,"w":"situations."},{"t":10.16,"w":"Hey,"},{"t":10.36,"w":"welcome"},{"t":10.64,"w":"to"},{"t":10.72,"w":"the"},{"t":10.8,"w":"shop."},{"t":11.2,"w":"So,"},{"t":11.4,"w":"we're"},{"t":11.6,"w":"going"},{"t":11.92,"w":"to"},{"t":12.12,"w":"look"},{"t":12.68,"w":"at"},{"t":13.36,"w":"one"},{"t":13.8,"w":"joint"},{"t":14.4,"w":"with"},{"t":14.8,"w":"three"},{"t":15.36,"w":"different"},{"t":16.84,"w":"settings"},{"t":17.56,"w":"and"},{"t":18.04,"w":"techniques"},{"t":19.04,"w":"here"},{"t":19.48,"w":"on"},{"t":19.72,"w":"this"},{"t":20.04,"w":"weld."},{"t":20.92,"w":"So,"},{"t":21.12,"w":"we're"},{"t":21.2,"w":"going"},{"t":21.32,"w":"to"},{"t":21.4,"w":"start"},{"t":21.68,"w":"off"},{"t":21.92,"w":"by"},{"t":22.08,"w":"running"},{"t":22.68,"w":"hot"},{"t":23.12,"w":"and"},{"t":23.28,"w":"fast"},{"t":23.72,"w":"in"},{"t":23.8,"w":"a"},{"t":23.84,"w":"straight"},{"t":24.36,"w":"line"},{"t":24.84,"w":"using"},{"t":25.16,"w":"the"},{"t":25.32,"w":"recommended"},{"t":26,"w":"settings"},{"t":26.6,"w":"on"},{"t":26.8,"w":"my"},{"t":26.96,"w":"Fronius."},{"t":27.56,"w":"Most"},{"t":27.8,"w":"European"},{"t":28.32,"w":"machines"},{"t":28.72,"w":"like"},{"t":28.96,"w":"